Files written for these tests, as an attacker might leave them. Addresses
are from the documentation ranges (RFC 5737) and domains are example.*;
the SSH keys were made for these tests and their private halves deleted.
systemd 257 (`systemd-analyze verify`), visudo and Debian's cron
(`crontab -n`) accept them, and OpenSSH's `sshd -t` the sshd snippet;
the at job is laid out as Debian 13's at 3.2.5 writes them.
